<title>SLOVENIA: Slovenia Revoz says 96 profit up 26 pct.</title>
<headline>Slovenia Revoz says 96 profit up 26 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LJUBLJANA 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Slovenian carmaker Revoz, a subsidiary of France's Renault, said on Friday 1996 net profit rose to 947 million tolars ($5.8 million) from 752.2 million in the previous year.</p>
<p>Revenue climbed to 139.8 billion tolars from 111.9 billion.</p>
<p>Revoz said revenue and profits improved mainly due to higher sales to the states of the former Yugoslavia and a six percent increase in sales to France.</p>
<p>Sales in Slovenia fell 5.3 percent.</p>
<p>-- Marja Novak, Ljubljana newsroom, 386-61-125-8439</p>
<p>($ = 163.3 Slovenian Tolars)</p>
</text>
